content:
Amy (Design): Quick mock attached — proposing a new dark theme variant I'm calling 'Inkwell'. focus: syntax saturation and chart legibility. screenshot: https://redwood.design/inkwell-proto.png
Jordan (Frontend): Nice! first impression: overall tones feel moody but code comments wash out on some monitors. can we bump comment + muted token? :eyes:
Amy (Design): Yeah noticed that on my laptop too. thinking of increasing muted saturation ~10% and slightly warming comments. also want charts to pop without clashing with syntax.
Matt (Eng-ML): For charts we should avoid chroma near accent to keep token highlighting distinct. propose a 6-color set for Series that passes 3:1 for small markers and 4.5:1 for text: [#6AD1FF, #7EE787, #FFD66B, #FF8BA1, #B4A6FF, #6EE0C6]
Kaela (Accessibility): Please run contrast checks. surface text vs panel needs >=4.5:1. low-contrast tokens like comments must be at least 3:1 if decorative only, otherwise 4.5:1. current muted (#9fb0c8) is borderline on #0e1624. suggest #a3b9c7 or increase weight.
Jordan (Frontend): Quick CSS vars I'm testing locally — copying here so y'all can tweak:
```css
:root {
  --bg: #0b1220;
  --panel: #0e1624;
  --text: #e6eef8;
  --muted: #a3b9c7; /* increased for contrast */
  --accent: #6ad1ff;
  --warn: #ffb86b;
  --ok: #7ee787;
  --syntax-fn: #ffd66b;
  --syntax-keyword: #d6b4ff;
  --syntax-string: #9fe5a8;
  --comment: #8ea0b4; /* warmer than before */
}
```
Amy (Design): Love that — comment color feels better. thoughts on code block bg? current #0f1115 reads almost black against app bg. maybe keep a subtle separation, e.g. #0b1220 bg and #0f1622 panel so blocks sit slightly lifted.
Matt (Eng-ML): Agree. also for streaming logs we need a slightly higher contrast for inline code tokens (monospace), otherwise telemetry is hard to scan on 4k. bump syntax-fn by ~8% luminance.
Kaela (Accessibility): Can we lock down target ratios? for main text >=4.5:1; code token labels >=3:1; charts with text overlays >=4.5:1. If you want, I can run a quick axe/contrast script and paste results.
Amy (Design): Yes please, that would be great. Jordan — if you push your vars to the PR branch I can update figma and check interactions. also copy tweak: the toggle should read 'Light / Inkwell' not 'Light / Dark' to avoid ambiguity in future variants.
Jordan (Frontend): will push in a sec. also added a small UX nicety::hover on color chips shows contrast ratio. snippet: `onclick => showContrast(hex)`  :thumbsup:
DesignBot: deploy-preview available at https://deploys.redwood.ai/preview/inkwell-1817654321 — snapshot build includes theme switcher and sample charts.
Matt (Eng-ML): saw the preview, charts look good, maybe desaturate series 2 slightly to keep focus on primary series.
Amy (Design): OK agreed — iterate series 2 in figma and I'll update tokens. Kaela can you run the accessibility script and drop results here?
Kaela (Accessibility): On it — running now, will paste results in ~10m.
Amy (Design): Thanks team — great progress. I'll open an issue with the decisions and link the PR when Jordan pushes. :sparkles:
